# JSDoc method descriptions

When adding or changing a function/method in JS, always write a **short description** in the JSDoc block above it — not only `@param` / `@returns`.

## Required

- One-line summary of what the method does (purpose, not implementation)
- Keep existing `@param`, `@returns`, and other tags
- Prefer Russian or English consistently with nearby code in the same file
- Trivial one-liners (e.g. simple getters that only return a field) may stay without a prose line if the name is self-explanatory — prefer a description for exported/public API

## Format

```javascript
/**
 * Load settings from chrome.storage.local with safe defaults.
 * @returns {Promise<{ defaultMinWidth: number, openaiApiKey: string, openaiModel: string }>}
 */
async function loadSettings() { /* ... */ }
```

## Avoid

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — tags only, no description
/**
 * @param {string} url
 * @returns {boolean}
 */
function isProductUrl(url) { /* ... */ }

// ✅ GOOD
/**
 * Check whether the URL looks like a Taobao/Tmall product page.
 * @param {string} url
 * @returns {boolean}
 */
function isProductUrl(url) { /* ... */ }
```

Do not invent long essays — one clear sentence is enough.
